## How sensitive is the case?

Lifetime value against churn, computed live: the curve is steep exactly where the
debate is, which is why a guess is expensive.

```{python}
#| echo: false
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

churn = np.linspace(0.02, 0.15, 100)
ltv = 2400 / churn / 1000     # LTV = ARR / churn, in $k

fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8.0, 2.9), tight_layout=True)
ax.plot(churn * 100, ltv, lw=2.6, color="#5b8cff")
ax.axvspan(5, 8, color="#e0566b", alpha=0.12)
ax.set_xlabel("monthly churn (%)")
ax.set_ylabel("LTV per seat ($k)")
ax.set_title("The 5–8% band (shaded) is where the meeting lives")
for s in ("top", "right"):
    ax.spines[s].set_visible(False)
plt.show()
```
